      "content": "that's a good start for the vibe, but it feels a little bit like a generic stump speech. i want to get deeper into his logic so the reader actually understands his worldview. can you make the monologue more specific? like, have him talk about how the current system is inherently broken and how his plan isn't just a choice, but a logical necessity to prevent total collapse. i want him to argue that anyone who disagrees is basically just ignoring reality or being bought off. make it feel intellectually heavy.",
